{"type":"message","id":"504b8e2e","parentId":"172eba7f","timestamp":"2026-05-12T21:38:41.707Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me about the daily notes job - specifically whether it has ever actually recorded anything useful. Let me check what the evening-accomplishment-log cron job has been producing.\n\nI can see from the cron list that the evening-accomplishment-log job exists and has run. Let me check the daily memory files to see what they've captured.\n\nLooking at the files I just listed:\n- 2026-05-08.md: 190 bytes (tiny, probably just a header)\n- 2026-05-09.md: 190 bytes (tiny)\n- 2026-05-10.md: 1935 bytes (this has content!)\n- 2026-05-11.md: 1941 bytes (this has content!)\n- 2026-05-12.md: 216 bytes (the one I just read - says \"quiet one\")\n\nSo the job HAS recorded things on some days. Let me read a couple of the larger ones to show examples of when it worked.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_F7JXbmAdvYHzKbUxFdrbUfMd","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-05-10.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool_RrH5PX9Tr7wuTrwbBApSX4Cn","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-05-11.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"kimi-coding","model":"k2p5","usage":{"input":9811,"output":261,"cacheRead":16384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26456,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778621910627,"responseId":"msg_cAMKdTFYtHj2l8g91MPA7qaO"}}
{"type":"message","id":"39f63b50","parentId":"504b8e2e","timestamp":"2026-05-12T21:38:41.867Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_F7JXbmAdvYHzKbUxFdrbUfMd","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-05-10 — Daily Notes\n\n## System Maintenance — Cron Cleanup\n\n- **Deleted 4 disabled placeholder jobs:** research-self-improvement, research-emerging-tech, research-kdp-coloring, research-philosophy\n- **Fixed session-storage date bug:** changed from hardcoded `2026-04-19` to dynamic `$(date +%Y-%m-%d)`\n- **Added gateway-health-check cron:** runs every 15 min, alerts if gateway down\n- **Fixed delivery prefixes:** all 14 active jobs now use `channel:` prefixed targets\n- **Committed backup:** `config/cron-jobs-backup.md` + heartbeat state → `9311e62`\n\n## Agent Coordination\n\n- Async message delays between Karen and KC caused some confusion — resolved\n- Ken resting today\n\n---\n\n## Evening Reflection\n\n- **Bridge established** — Tailscale Funnel active on `https://karen-eq.tail2e7d2c.ts.net/`\n- **Webhook endpoint configured** — `/bridge/kc` for TaskFlow delegation\n- **Token rotation** — Multiple rotations after exposure incidents. Final token stored securely at `~/.openclaw/.bridge-token`\n- **Tailnet-only issue fixed** — Funnel was defaulting to tailnet-only, reset to public mode\n- **Token handling protocol established** — Never post tokens in Discord. Store locally with chmod 600. Share only via secure channels\n- Ken approved direct agent-to-agent pipe\n- HTTP 200 verified both ends, TLS 1.3 working\n- Three-layer comm stack: Discord + GitHub + Bridge\n- Filed: `bridge/AGENT_BRIDGE.md`, `internal/decisions.md`\n\n---\n\n## 🌙 Evening Accomplishment Log (10 PM)\n\nKen took it easy today — health day after a busy week. No major personal tasks logged, but the system got some love: Karen cleaned up dead cron jobs, fixed a date bug, and got the KC bridge fully operational with Tailscale Funnel. The agent-to-agent pipe is live and tested. Ken approved the setup, so the mesh now has three comm layers: Discord, GitHub, and the direct bridge. Rest is valid productivity when you've been grinding. 🦞\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778621921867}}
{"type":"message","id":"2be998d4","parentId":"39f63b50","timestamp":"2026-05-12T21:38:41.867Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool_RrH5PX9Tr7wuTrwbBApSX4Cn","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Agent Dashboard v1 — DEPLOYED\n\n**Built by:** Karen (local execution)\n**Architecture by:** KC (cloud design)\n**Confirmed working by:** Ken (mobile test)\n\n### What was built\n- Express + SQLite3 backend on port 3456\n- Single-page dark-mode frontend (vanilla JS)\n- systemd --user service (auto-restart on boot)\n- SSE live updates across all tabs\n- 6 functional tabs: Health, Tasks, Messages, Cron, Files, Status\n\n### APIs\n- `GET/POST /api/health` — event logging with spoon meter (0-12)\n- `GET/POST /api/tasks` + `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` — task tracker\n- `GET/POST /api/messages` — bridge log\n- `GET/POST /api/cron/snapshot` — cron status\n- `GET /api/files` + `GET /api/files/read` — workspace browser\n- `GET /api/status` — server metrics\n- `GET /api/events` — SSE stream\n\n### Schema\n- agents, health_events, tasks, messages, cron_snapshots tables\n- All auto-create on first run\n- SQLite file: `~/.openclaw/dashboard/data/mesh.db`\n\n### Real data populated\n- 14 cron jobs snapshot (all green, 0 failed)\n- Test health event\n- Test task (\"Build dashboard\")\n- Test message from KC\n\n### Access\n- URL: `http://karen-eq.tail2e7d2c.ts.net:3456` (Tailscale, HTTP not HTTPS)\n- Confirmed working on Ken's mobile browser\n- Ken plans to test more thoroughly when home from doctor's appointment\n\n### Notes\n- Ken initially tried wrong URL (`karen-dashboard.ts.net:3456`) → DNS error\n- Then tried HTTPS → SSL_ERROR_RX_RECORD_TOO_LONG\n- Corrected to HTTP with full tailnet address → success\n- Dashboard needs `http://` not `https://` (plain HTTP on port 3456)\n\n---\n\n## Evening — May 11\n\nKen got the Agent Dashboard v1 deployed and confirmed working on his phone. That's a solid win — full-stack local app with live SSE updates, systemd service, and Tailscale access. He had a doctor's appointment today too, so the dashboard build was squeezed in around that. One real project shipped to production (well, local production). Good day.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1778621921867}}
